-- The average of a set of intervals is an interval of the same unit
200	IntervalMillisecond
-- Every interval kind
2	IntervalNanosecond
2	IntervalMicrosecond
2	IntervalMillisecond
2	IntervalSecond
2	IntervalMinute
2	IntervalHour
2	IntervalDay
2	IntervalWeek
2	IntervalMonth
2	IntervalQuarter
2	IntervalYear
-- A fractional average is rounded half to even, as for the date and time types
100
102
-100
-102
-- The division is exact above the range where Float64 holds every integer
2305843009213693953
-- An empty input gives a zero-length interval, as an empty input gives the epoch for a date
0	IntervalDay
-- A single row
7
-- Nullable
20	Nullable(IntervalSecond)
\N	Nullable(IntervalSecond)
-- Combinators
4	IntervalSecond
3	IntervalMinute
3	IntervalMinute
1	IntervalSecond
[4,5]	Array(IntervalDay)
2	IntervalHour
-- GROUP BY
0	4
1	4
2	5
-- The average of an interval can be added to a date
2026-01-01 00:00:05
